## Spec docs/errors/E1115.md / docs/specs/types/async_lowering.spec.md
## ("Out of scope" §): `.await` inside the body of a `loop` /
## `while` / `while let` / `for` block is rejected at type-check
## time with code E1115. v1 lowering builds a flat
## `[await_let]* tail` state machine; per-iteration loop suspension
## requires re-constructing the awaitee on each iteration and
## restoring the right state on resume — deferred to v2.

async def fetch() -> Int
  42
end

async def handler() -> Int
  let var sum = 0
  loop
    let v = fetch().await
    sum = sum + v
    if sum > 100
      break sum
    end
  end
end

def main
  let r = block_on(handler())
  puts "#{r}"
end
